# JeRyu Web Forge — Final Patch-Style Engineering Diff

This file is intentionally a patch-style engineering diff, not a claim that every hunk has already been applied and compiled in this sandbox. It is written against the current repo shape observed on 2026-05-26 and is organized so an engineer can apply it as the first production web-forge patch set, then fill provider-specific methods behind the new traits and handlers.

Key direction:

1. Preserve the current Rust CLI/TUI/control-plane architecture.
2. Replace the `apps/web` UX-QA-only package with a real Vite/React/TypeScript application while keeping UX-QA scripts.
3. Add `src/web` for Axum REST/WebSocket/static serving.
4. Add `src/web_events` for resumable realtime activity.
5. Add forge DTOs under `src/api` and domain services under `src/repos`, `src/repo_browser`, and `src/merge`.
6. Add safe Markdown rendering via `comrak` + `ammonia` so `README.md` and every `.md` blob render to sanitized HTML.
7. Extend `GitHost` toward full GitHub/GitLab repository, file, ref, issue, review, and settings parity.

